⚠️ severity: IMPORTANT —
⚠️ **IMPORTANT: `routeOne` has no `ACTION_DIFFERENTIAL` branch — the hardened re-request verdict lands in the red-on-old lane**

`triageDifferentialOutcome` was deliberately hardened in this PR (gh-1354): only `green|red` decide — `unavailable`/null/`''` now return `ACTION_DIFFERENTIAL` ("re-requests the rerun and never decides on incomplete evidence"). But this dispatcher — the function's only production consumer — was not taught that value: `routeOne` handles BOUNCE/ESCALATE and the new REWORK branch, then falls everything else straight into the red-on-old maintenance route.

If an `ACTION_DIFFERENTIAL` verdict ever reaches here:

- `maintenanceEntry` stamps `entry.evidence = { differential: 'red' }` — a fabricated record for an outcome that never ran;
- `routes.maintained` renders the report section "ran the failing TC on its last-green build and it fails there too — the failure predates the change" — the exact false claim the hardening exists to make impossible;
- `dispatchResult` lists the TC in `maintainedTestCases` while the entry verdict (`differential-rerun`) simultaneously re-parks it — the digest then shows both a red-on-old claim and a parked request for the same finding.

Today this is unreachable (`runDifferential` returns only `green|red`; `unavailable` returns earlier), so no live bug — but the contract mismatch sits inside this PR's own two changed files, on the fail-safe property ("never decides on incomplete evidence") the PR claims to strengthen. Suggested fix — keep the fail-safe symmetric:

```javascript
if (verdict.action === tcTriage.ACTION_DIFFERENTIAL) {
    // the hardened continuation refused to decide — re-park, never a red-on-old claim
    vars.ledger = tcMaintenanceLedger.appendFinding(vars.ledger, unavailableBump(request, 'incomplete outcome — re-requesting the rerun'));
    routes.stalled.push({ tcKey: request.tcKey, detail: 'incomplete differential outcome' });
    return;
}
```

